     9	profile is **[assumption]**, "named in Layer 2 and discharged as H1a evidence: exact library and version, accepted
    10	signature encodings, public-key validation behavior, low-order-point handling, cofactor equation variant, and
    11	negative test vectors for each, all recorded in the repository." The [model] half is `formal/suite/s-p3/`.
    12	
    13	**Run it** (from `service/verifier`):
    14	
    15	```
    16	.venv/bin/python -m pytest -q ../../formal/p3-verification-profile/test_p3_profile.py
    17	```
    18	
    19	| File | Contents |
    20	|---|---|
    21	| `vectors/F1-library.json` | library, version, OpenSSL build, wheel tag and binding digest, the four exact calls |
    22	| `vectors/F2-signature-encodings.json` | 65 signature vectors: rule-O encodings (O-01..O-25), rule-O policy (P-01..P-06, P-10..P-25), rule R (R-01..R-18) |
    23	| `vectors/F3-public-key-validation.json` | 37 key vectors (K-01..K-37) |
    24	| `vectors/F4-low-order-points.json` | 8 key vectors (L-01..L-08) |
    25	| `vectors/F5-equation-variant.json` | 11 equation/message-representative vectors (E-01..E-11) and the key-substitution pair (D-01, D-02) |
    26	| `test_p3_profile.py` | vector harness, permissive-backend tests, library characterization, bundle tests, wheel identity |
